Towards the end of the Middle Ages, Western Europe began to develop its own style. As one of the most significant advances of the era, people began to use buttons to fasten clothes.
Self-sufficiency is farming that produces enough food only to support the farmer and his family.
Self-suffering economy is a simple, often organic system that uses natural seeds for the eco-area, combined with crop rotation or other relatively simple ways to maximize the harvest.
Historically, most farmers engaged in self-sufficiency farming, and this is still the case in many developing countries.
Subcultures bring together like-minded people who feel that they are rejected by society's norms, so that they are able to develop their own identity.
Subcultures may be distinguished by age, ethnicity, social class, place and/or the gender of members.
Qualities that define the subculture as their own and separately may be linguistic, aesthetic, religious, political, gender or sexual, geographical, or a combination of a variety of factors.
Often, members of the sub-culture communicate their membership with distinctive and symbolic use of style, which includes fashion, manners and their own slang.
