Dangerous weather is a general term for all dangerous weather phenomena that can cause damage, serious social disturbance or loss of life.
Dangerous weather can occur all over the world, and there are different types that may depend on geography, topography and atmospheric conditions.
Strong winds, hail, high precipitation and wildfires are forms and consequences of dangerous weather, as are thunderstorms, whirlwinds, water columns and cyclones.
Dangerous weather regional and seasonal phenomena include blizzards, ice storms and sandstorms.
It is strongly recommended that passengers be aware of the threat of dangerous weather that affects their destination, as it may affect their travel plans.
